# Format after edits

After changing any `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, or `.jsx` file, run ESLint `--fix` on those files before finishing:

```
yarn eslint --max-warnings=0 --ext .js,.ts,.tsx --fix <files>
```

If `yarn` is not on PATH (common on Windows), use `corepack yarn` with the same args.

Do not hand-wrap lines or guess object/JSX spacing. Prettier owns spaces inside `{ }`, trailing commas, and line breaks. Hand-edited style like `style={{paddingTop: "2px" }}` fails `prettier/prettier`.

Treat leftover `prettier/prettier` as a failed edit. Run the command above and re-check the file.
